title: Authorizations › Case page › Draft › Review, sign and what happens next
route: /authorizations/case/R-1042?tab=draft
intro: What happens when a person leaves the Draft tab to send the request: the gate, the hand-off to New Case where a clinician signs, and where the request appears once it is sent.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the payer receiving the request is simulated. The summary signed in New Case is the one on this tab: edits, applied actions and added clinical context are all in it.
---
start s1 "On the Draft tab: read the summary and the four checks"
decision dc "Do all four checks pass, and is the request still preparing?"
process off "'Send to payer' is off\nThe reason sits under the button, e.g. 'Integrity has 2 open checks. Apply the matching actions first.'"
click sp "Click 'Send to payer' (large button)"
click os "Click 'Open in review and sign' (header button)"
process rp "The case page finds this request's draft in New Case, or makes one from the request\nThe draft opens at Review & submit when the request is ready, at Authorization preparation when agents still have work"
process ns "Nothing is sent yet\n'Nothing goes to the payer until a clinician signs.'"
goto gR "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Review & submit › Sign and send to payer"

group gSign "In New Case (summary only, drawn in its own diagram)"
  process sg "A licensed clinician signs with 'Sign and send to payer'\nThe UR coordinator cannot sign; Dr. Rivera can"
  ext py "Navigator sends the request through the payer's portal\n(demo: simulated)"
  doc pk "What goes out\nThe signed summary and the packet's documents"
endgroup

store rq "Dashboard: the request is created, or moves to 'Received'\nHistory: 'You signed as Dr. Rivera (clinician) and sent the request', 'Navigator sent the request through the payer's portal', 'Navigator saved the receipt to the case' (read in the case page's History)"
toast tt "Toast 'Sent to the payer'\n'R-0988 is on the Dashboard as Received.'"
toast nt "Notification from Navigator: 'Sent to the payer'\n'R-0988 was sent. It now shows as Received on the Dashboard.'"
screen db "Dashboard opens on that request\nStage 'Received'"
process qg "Back in the queue the request is gone\nThe open count drops by one\nThe sidebar badge too, if it was in Act now or Due within 24 hours"
process cp "The case page of a sent request shows the request's own status\n'Next:' the Dashboard's step, and a disabled 'Sent to payer' in place of 'Send to payer'\nHistory lists the signature and the send"
goto gD "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Open and read a request"
goto gQ "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Open the queue and read the top"

s1 --> dc
dc -->|No| off
dc -->|Yes| sp --> rp
s1 --> os --> rp
rp --> ns --> gR
gR --> sg --> py --> pk
sg --> rq
rq --> tt
rq --> nt
rq --> db --> gD
rq --> qg --> gQ
qg -.-> cp
